[Music]  22 minutes after the hour and just when  it seemed like le'veon bell was  potentially going to sit out the whole  season or at a minimum show up the  tuesday after week 10 the latest he  could  jeremy fowler of espn reports that bell  will show up in week seven that's the  steelers bye week sign the franchise  tender and bell plans to stay with the  steelers after that bell later told  fowler it sucks having to sit out  football i want to play i want to win  games and the playoffs but i've got to  take this stand knowing my worth and  knowing i can tear a ligament or get  surgery at any time i knew i couldn't  play 16 games with 400 or more touches  now peter we saw on  on sunday what can happen with one play  you can break your leg if you're earl  thomas he's still coming back belle is  and accepting the risk that he will  suffer the kind of injury that will keep  him from getting the kind of payday that  he wants so  i don't know  is this  bell making a calculated decision that  i'm gonna miss half the season and just  roll the dice on the second half or did  he just get to the point where he  decides i can't stay away anymore i want  to be back it sounds like he's he's  mainly decided i just want to be back  and play football  mike this is a calculated risk he's  basically saying  i'm going to get paid for a little more  than half the season and i'm going to  play for a little more than half the  season remember  the nfl distributes paychecks in 17 part  increments not 16. so theoretically and  i wonder if the steelers would grieve  this  if he signs his tender on the monday of  the bye week  theoretically i would think i don't know  exactly what the rules are  but i would think he's going to get paid  in that bye week you know uh basically  800 whatever it is 853 000  that's a pretty expensive check uh you  know for the steelers to write when the  team is not playing and i don't even  think the team will be practicing that  week so that's one part of it  the other part i find really interesting  is that right now james connor has taken  his place as 81 touches through four  games so that means basically that the  steelers are giving the le'veon bell  character in their little mini series  20 touches a game that adds up to about  325 a year in general okay and i'm not  saying that this is exact right but the  only point that i'm making is that  you never know  like le'veon bell says i don't want to  come back for 400 touches first of all  i don't think there's any way anyway  with a healthy james connor  that if le'veon bell was there for 16  games fully healthy that he would have  ever had 400 touches i just i don't see  the steelers doing that i see it being  290 to  150 something like that that's just it's  an absolute guess  but the second thing is mike have you  looked at the steelers schedule  the first two games out of the buy  cleveland  and at baltimore  so le'veon bell comes back all of a  sudden it's no longer a gimme game  against the browns  he comes back to play the browns and  then they go to the ravens in what i  think is going to be an absolute total  must win game for the cleveland bro for  the pittsburgh steelers  here's another issue to keep in mind and  this came up back in early september  when he didn't show up before the final  roster cuts by rule after that if he  decides to sign his franchise tender he  and the steelers must decide in advance  what he will be paid if the steelers put  him on roster exempt status which they  can do for two regular season games i  don't know whether or not they're going  to insist on doing that when he shows up  in week seven but if they have the  ability to put him on roster exempt  status for two games and they're in a  bye week in week seven and they have to  agree what he's going to be paid while  he's on roster exempt status while  they're getting him in shape  that could get very interesting he may  have every intention to show up that  week and then he shows up and kevin  colbert says to him okay we got to  figure out what we're going to pay you  while you're on roster exempt we're  putting you on a two-week roster  exemption and he's like what are you  talking about well we're not going to  pay 855 000 a week if we're going to  exercise our right to put you on roster  exempt status so we have to figure out  how much we're going to pay you that's  the side of this we don't know yet peter  because we don't know whether or not the  steelers are going to roll out the red  carpet they've been trying to trade him  so how are they going to react to this  that remains to be seen but it could  still get a little messy when he shows  up  i expect it to be messy there's no way  this is going to be clear or clean i  don't think it's going to be an earl  atomic earl thomas seahawks type of  messi but i do think there's a good  chance it'll be messy and mike i just  keep saying  the steelers at that point are going to  be in must win mode and i think mike  tomlin's attitude is going to be we'll  let bygones be by guns we got to beat  the browns and the ravens hi i'm mike  tarico and thanks for watching make sure  to hit subscribe for the latest news and  highlights from nbc sports

